From cd58c1bc0724d958aca3fd446a2a8f542cd886a3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Maxime=20M=C3=A9r=C3=A9?= <maxime.mere@foss.st.com>
Date: Tue, 11 Aug 2026 16:18:55 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 894/913] drivers: stm32_cpu_opp: fix off-by-one in
 stm32_cpu_opp_set_rate()
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

When no OPP matches the requested rate, the search loop leaves
opp == cpu_opp.opp_count, but the bounds check only rejected
opp > cpu_opp.opp_count, letting that out-of-range index through
to set_opp() and reading one entry past the end of cpu_opp.dvfs[].

Reject opp == cpu_opp.opp_count as well, matching the equivalent
check already used in stm32_cpu_opp_set_level().

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [ST downstream https://github.com/STMicroelectronics/optee_os.git a4760dbbb98dc86fc7e6779b9a0c8b03d623dcac drivers: stm32_cpu_opp: fix off-by-one in stm32_cpu_opp_set_rate()]
Assisted-by: GitHub-Copilot:Claude-Sonnet-5
Signed-off-by: Maxime Méré <maxime.mere@foss.st.com>
Change-Id: I0e38ba374fe51aa6260435b837ad5f183aca966b
Reviewed-on: https://gerrit.st.com/c/mpu/oe/optee/optee_os/+/598512
Reviewed-by: Thomas BOURGOIN <thomas.bourgoin@foss.st.com>
Domain-Review: Patrick DELAUNAY <patrick.delaunay@foss.st.com>
ACI: CITOOLS <MDG-smet-aci-reviews@list.st.com>
ACI: CIBUILD <MDG-smet-aci-builds@list.st.com>
---
 core/drivers/stm32_cpu_opp.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/core/drivers/stm32_cpu_opp.c b/core/drivers/stm32_cpu_opp.c
index fbab04008..bcbfa717a 100644
--- a/core/drivers/stm32_cpu_opp.c
+++ b/core/drivers/stm32_cpu_opp.c
@@ -456,7 +456,7 @@ TEE_Result stm32_cpu_opp_set_rate(unsigned int rate)
 		if (cpu_opp.dvfs[opp].freq_khz == rate_khz)
 			break;
 
-	if (opp > cpu_opp.opp_count)
+	if (opp >= cpu_opp.opp_count)
 		return TEE_ERROR_BAD_PARAMETERS;
 
 	/* set OPP: configure clock and voltage with SoC function */
-- 
